Description:
Description

Build the future with us

Are you passionate about data and creating value? Would you like to contribute to decisions that shape the future of individual insurance?

As a Data Analyst within the Strategy and Analytics team in the Pricing, New Business and Claims division, you will play a central role in advancing our business intelligence capabilities. You will collaborate with data analysts, managers, pricing and claims specialists, and other business partners to transform data into performance drivers.

This position is a great opportunity to showcase your skills and fully realize your potential within a caring and trustworthy company. Here, people and their development are at the heart of our priorities, fostering an environment that encourages collaboration and innovation.

What You’ll Accomplish With Us

As a Data Analyst, you’ll be at the core of our mission. Here are the main responsibilities:


Design, develop and optimize business intelligence tools to support business decisions;
Contribute to risk management controls and market analyses;
Translate business needs into practical, tailored and well-documented solutions;
Analyze data and recommend key performance indicators;
Actively participate in the governance of business intelligence assets;
Contribute to the quality of information data;
Support business partners in identifying and defining their needs by highlighting available data and value-creation opportunities.


What Could Accelerate Your Success In This Role

We’re looking for someone who:


Holds a bachelor’s degree in statistics, actuarial science, business intelligence or another related field;
Has at least two years of relevant experience in data analysis, business intelligence or a similar role;
Is proficient in SQL and a data visualization tool such as Power BI or Tableau;
Demonstrates strong analytical thinking and the ability to analyze complex data;
Communicates technical concepts effectively to business partners with varied backgrounds;
Demonstrates autonomy, initiative and rigour, particularly in validation and documentation;
Has a strong interest in technology and the ability to learn and use new tools and programming languages;
Has experience in the insurance or financial services industry. Knowledge of a programming language used in data analysis, such as Python or R, is considered an asset.


Why you’ll love working with us


A work environment where learning and development merge with a collective pursuit of excellence;
AI is in everyone’s hands, empowering you to increase your personal effectiveness while supporting the organization’s growth;
A healthy, safe, fair and inclusive environment where potential can be freely expressed and developed;
The opportunity to work in a hybrid environment, supported by flexibility and access to inspiring and innovative workspaces.


Competitive Benefits


Flexible group insurance plans;
Competitive retirement savings plan and employee share purchase plan;
Vacation program, wellness days and personal development days;
Telemedicine services;
Employee and Family Assistance Program;
Ergonomic furniture program;
Performance bonus;
Discounts on iA products, and much more!


Apply now and get ahead in your career, where your talent really belongs!

Still unsure about applying?

At iA, we believe in potential and value diverse experiences. If this role inspires you, go ahead and apply. Your place might be with us, and we want to get to know you!
